REST route (src/actix/api/collections_api.rs:94-109):
#[get("/collections/{collection_name}/aliases")]
async fn get_collection_aliases(
    dispatcher: web::Data<Dispatcher>,
    collection: Path<CollectionPath>,
    ActixAuth(auth): ActixAuth,
) -> HttpResponse {
    // No request to verify
    let pass = new_unchecked_verification_pass();
    helpers::time(do_list_collection_aliases(
        dispatcher.toc(&auth, &pass),
        &auth,
        &collection.collection_name,
    ))
    .await
}

Handler (src/common/collections.rs:167-188) — auth only, NO existence check:
pub async fn do_list_collection_aliases(
    toc: &TableOfContent,
    auth: &Auth,
    collection_name: &str,
) -> Result<CollectionsAliasesResponse, StorageError> {
    let collection_pass = auth.check_collection_access(
        collection_name,
        AccessRequirements::new(),
        "list_collection_aliases",
    )?;
    let access = auth.unlogged_access(); // Do not log as it is just logger above
    let aliases: Vec<AliasDescription> = toc
        .collection_aliases(&collection_pass, access)
        .await?
        .into_iter()
        .map(|alias| AliasDescription {
            alias_name: alias,
            collection_name: collection_name.to_string(),
        })
        .collect();
    Ok(CollectionsAliasesResponse { aliases })
}

check_collection_access (lib/storage/src/rbac/mod.rs:138-150) returns CollectionPass for ANY name under global access — AccessRequirements::new() imposes nothing and no existence test occurs.

toc.collection_aliases (toc/mod.rs:433-450) — scans the alias map only:
    pub async fn collection_aliases(
        &self,
        collection_pass: &CollectionPass<'_>,
        access: &Access,
    ) -> Result<Vec<String>, StorageError> {
        let mut result = self
            .alias_persistence
            .read()
            .await
            .collection_aliases(collection_pass.name());
        result.retain(|alias| {
            access
                .check_collection_access(alias, AccessRequirements::new())
                .is_ok()
        });
        Ok(result)
    }

alias lookup (alias_mapping.rs:114-122) — empty Vec for any name without matching target:
    pub fn collection_aliases(&self, collection_name: &str) -> Vec<String> {
        let mut result = vec![];
        for (alias, target_collection) in self.alias_mapping.0.iter() {
            if collection_name == target_collection {
                result.push(alias.clone());
            }
        }
        result
    }

CONTRAST — the existence-checked machinery exists and is used by sibling faces (describe/count) that returned 404 in the log: resolve_name (toc/mod.rs:407-419) ends with `collections.validate_collection_exists(&resolved_name)?;` and validate_collection_exists (collections_ops.rs:25-32) raises StorageError::not_found(format!("Collection `{collection_name}` doesn't exist!")) — the exact 404 body seen in the log controls. do_list_collection_aliases never calls get_collection/resolve_name/validate_collection_exists.

gRPC face shares the identical handler (src/tonic/api/collections_api.rs:132-152, list_collection_aliases -> do_list_collection_aliases) — same absence, no REST/gRPC asymmetry at code level.

Drop cascade: collection_meta_ops.rs:217-220 calls alias_persistence.remove_collection(collection_name) (alias_mapping.rs:82-93 retain v != collection_name) — dropped collections keep no alias entries, so the post-drop listing returns 200 {"result":{"aliases":[]}} from an empty map rather than 404.
